id: pm-d2wfig
title: "Derived scheduling: propagate milestone deadlines backward through the ordering graph so every gating item carries a latest-start date instead of only six dates existing in the whole plan"
description: ""
type: Feature
status: open
priority: 1
tags[5]: analytics,governance,graph,planning,scheduling
created_at: "2026-08-13T08:53:22.763Z"
updated_at: "2026-08-13T08:53:57.276Z"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 720
acceptance_criteria: "Latest-start dates are derived for every item on an ordering path to a dated item, from that item's deadline and the estimates on the path, and are reported as derived rather than stored as authored deadlines; Slack is reported in time units alongside the existing topological layer slack, so an item with layer slack and no date slack is distinguishable from one with both; A path whose accumulated estimates cannot fit between now and the gated deadline is reported as an over-committed path, naming the deadline, the path and the shortfall; Items with no estimate are reported as an explicit unschedulable residual rather than being treated as zero-duration, so the derivation never silently manufactures feasibility; Derivation is bounded and stays inside the graph analytics token and latency budgets at million-item scale, and degrades to a declared partial result rather than a full scan; A negative control proves the over-commitment finding fires when a deadline is moved earlier than its path allows and clears when it is moved back"
goal: explainable-graph
objective: "Any dated commitment implies a dated constraint on every item that gates it, computed from the recorded graph rather than asserted item by item"
value: "A plan whose only dates sit on its endpoints cannot be late until it already is. Six dates across 339 open items means no item can ever report as at-risk, and the earliest possible warning is the milestone date itself."
impact: "Turns the six outcome milestones from declared intent into a schedule the record can check, and gives every relevance and next-work signal a real urgency input instead of a priority integer."
outcome: "Latest-start and slack are reported in dates for every item on a path to a dated commitment, derived and reproducible, and a path whose estimates no longer fit its deadline is a finding rather than a surprise."
why_now: "The milestone ladder now carries deadlines from 2026-10-31 to 2028-06-30 and a coherent blocker DAG, so the inputs for derivation exist for the first time; the analytic that would consume them computes in layers and ignores dates."
parent: pm-96h7
risk: medium
confidence: 85
