  pm-xp1xsw,implements,"2026-08-13T08:53:22.763Z","harness:claude-code","cli:create:dep",detected
body: "## The census\n\nOpen items (open, in_progress, blocked, draft): 339. Carrying a deadline: 6. Those six are exactly the outcome milestones. Every other open item is undated.\n\nThe nineteen items that directly gate the six milestones by `blocked_by` — pm-pbyu, pm-1kxs, pm-usfg, pm-xpumg4, pm-9yfo, pm-9rxu, pm-2sbj8p, pm-atfm, pm-tch9cs, pm-4k6b, pm-agou, pm-zclzll, pm-rtn5h6, pm-pae3wo, pm-ygli86, pm-8jdc, pm-li2fj5, pm-nfrhf0, pm-t8a0x1 — carry no deadline between them.\n\n## The plan that exists and is coherent\n\nThe milestone layer is genuinely well formed, which is why derivation is now possible:\n\n| milestone | deadline | est. min | gated by |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| pm-j82fd3 command grammar | 2026-10-31 | 4,800 | pbyu, 1kxs |\n| pm-9rgaal SDK-complete core | 2026-12-31 | 6,000 | j82fd3, usfg, xpumg4 |\n| pm-w7ccmv provable history | 2027-03-31 | 5,400 | 9yfo |\n| pm-o87av6 proven scale | 2027-09-30 | 9,600 | 9rgaal, 9rxu, 2sbj8p, atfm, tch9cs, 4k6b |\n| pm-xp1xsw v1.0 GA contract | 2027-12-31 | 3,600 | 9rgaal, agou, j82fd3, w7ccmv, o87av6, zclzll, rtn5h6, pae3wo, ygli86 |\n| pm-t4d7nz universal platform | 2028-06-30 | 12,000 | 9rgaal, w7ccmv, o87av6, xp1xsw, 8jdc, li2fj5, nfrhf0, t8a0x1 |\n\nEvery milestone's deadline is later than every milestone that gates it, so the dated layer is internally consistent. The ordering is a genuine DAG, not a ring. The estimates are present. All three inputs a backward pass needs are already recorded.\n\n## Why the existing analytic cannot answer it\n\n`pm graph slack` on this tracker reports `makespan: 10`, `scheduled_count: 560`, `critical_count: 22`, `critical_path_length: 9`. Those are topological layers. The unit is hops, not time. So the surface that computes slack cannot read the six deadlines, and the six deadlines constrain nothing the surface computes.\n\nThe consequence is that \"critical\" currently means \"on the longest chain of hops\", which is not the same as \"on the path that will miss its date\". An item can sit on a nine-hop critical path with two years of date slack, and an item one hop from a milestone can be the only thing that will actually be late. Today those rank identically.\n\n## Boundary, so this does not become date fabrication\n\nThe derivation must produce *derived latest-start*, never an authored `deadline`. Writing dates onto 333 items would create a second schedule to disagree with the first, and would make the numbers unfalsifiable — exactly the failure mode a hand-maintained ledger always produces. The dates stay computed, the inputs stay the recorded deadline plus the recorded estimates plus the recorded edges, and an item with no estimate is reported as unschedulable rather than assumed instantaneous.\n\nThat residual is large today and should be visible from the first run: estimates exist widely, but the 915 items missing `estimated_minutes` across all statuses are exactly the population that would otherwise be silently treated as free."
